  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize your Wild cards. Since they change every round, never get too attached to a specific rank. A '3' is a treasure in Round 1 but just an annoyance in Round 2. Use your Wilds to bridge gaps in Runs (e.g., 4-Wild-6).\n\nThe 'Last Turn' Warning: When an opponent goes out, you only have one move left. If you have high-value cards (Aces, Kings, Wilds) that aren't melded, discard them IMMEDIATELY. It is better to have an incomplete run of 3s than a loose King.\n\nDiscard Pile Psychology: Don't pick up a card from the discard pile unless it NATURALLY completes a meld. Picking up a discard tells your opponents exactly what suit or rank you are building, allowing them to 'block' you by holding the remaining cards of that set.",
    Player: "Prioritize your Wild cards. Since they change every round, never get too attached to a specific rank. A '3' is a treasure in Round 1 but just an annoyance in Round 2. Use your Wilds to bridge gaps in Runs (e.g., 4-Wild-6).\n\nThe 'Last Turn' Warning: When an opponent goes out, you only have one move left. If you have high-value cards (Aces, Kings, Wilds) that aren't melded, discard them IMMEDIATELY. It is better to have an incomplete run of 3s than a loose King.\n\nDiscard Pile Psychology: Don't pick up a card from the discard pile unless it NATURALLY completes a meld. Picking up a discard tells your opponents exactly what suit or rank you are building, allowing them to 'block' you by holding the remaining cards of that set.",
